.DS_Store

# Eagle auto-backups
*.s#?
*.b#?

# Fusion exports / fab outputs (regenerate, don't track)
gerbers/
*.zip

# Build artifacts (regenerate with `make`)
emulator/p8xemu
emulator/*.o
compiler/p8cc-host.bin

# stray microcode images if a generator is run from the repo root
/u?.bin
/u?.hex
microcode/u?.hex
emulator/u?.bin
/os/run-disk.img
/os/run-disk1.img

# generated by tools/mkbacklogpdf.py (re-run it; do not track the artifact)
BACKLOG-summary.pdf

# Eagle/ libraries + design rules ARE tracked (so the project is self-contained
# for anyone reproducing it). Skip only the redundant pre-conversion binary backup.
Eagle/Libraries/*.orig.lbr

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# emulator/test/ — ALLOW-LIST, not a deny-list.
#
# The tests write their scratch files next to their sources: images, compiled
# .bin/.asm twins, preprocessed .c, traces, tokens, ASTs. Listing each one by
# name did not scale — this section reached ~200 lines with six duplicates, and
# it still leaked: generated .asm twins were tracked, went stale, and silently
# made the os_cmdbuild byte-compare check an out-of-date build.
#
# So: ignore everything here by default and name the hand-written sources. A new
# generated file is then ignored automatically, and the failure mode flips from
# "silently tracked and stale" to "git does not see my new source", which is
# obvious the first time you commit.
#
# Adding a hand-written test source? Follow the naming convention (*.sh,
# h*.asm, test*.asm) or add an explicit ! line below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
emulator/test/*
!emulator/test/*.sh
!emulator/test/test*.asm
!emulator/test/eq.inc
# The BIOS/FS hand-written probes. Named individually on purpose: `h*.asm` also
# matches the GENERATED head.asm (the head-command twin), and `Makefile.*` also
# matches the generated Makefile.C.
!emulator/test/h.asm
!emulator/test/hdel.asm
!emulator/test/hdir.asm
!emulator/test/hfs.asm
!emulator/test/hilba.asm
!emulator/test/hnorm.asm
!emulator/test/hopen.asm
!emulator/test/hresolve.asm
!emulator/test/hwrdir.asm
!emulator/test/hwrite.asm
!emulator/test/Makefile.A
!emulator/test/Makefile.S
# Orphan: matches no test and is referenced nowhere — looks like an accidental
# Finder duplicate of the generated prog.asm. Kept tracked only so this change
# is behaviour-preserving; safe to delete.
!emulator/test/prog 2.asm
